  "version": 1,
  "_comment": "Journal registry for Evidence Digest. 'ta' is the MEDLINE title abbreviation used in PubMed's [ta] field - the only reliable journal identifier, since full titles and ISSNs both drift. 'specialty' must match a specialty slug in pipeline/config/taxonomy/*.json and determines the catch-all topic when no rule fires. 'tier' feeds the importance score only. 'scope':'all' takes every newly indexed paper; 'scope':'topic' additionally requires topicFilter to match, which is how broad multidisciplinary journals are kept to their clinically relevant output. Always run `python -m evidence_digest.cli check` after editing: any journal returning 0 hits over a 120-day window almost certainly has a wrong 'ta'.",

  "topicFilter": "(patient*[tiab] OR clinical[tiab] OR clinician*[tiab] OR disease*[tiab] OR diagnos*[tiab] OR therap*[tiab] OR treatment*[tiab] OR trial[tiab] OR cohort[tiab] OR mortality[tiab] OR morbidity[tiab] OR cancer*[tiab] OR tumour*[tiab] OR tumor*[tiab] OR health[tiab] OR healthcare[tiab] OR medicine[tiab] OR medical[tiab] OR hospital*[tiab] OR physician*[tiab] OR nurs*[tiab])",

